UN Investigative Mandates
https://helenarbc.github.io/un-investigative-mandates/

WHAT THIS COVERS

This notice covers the whole of this work, namely:

  (a) the site code — HTML, CSS, JavaScript, the chart routines and the build
      scripts;
  (b) the coding scheme — the variable definitions, the typology of mandates,
      the inclusion test and the codebook;
  (c) the coded dataset — the records, the identified operative paragraphs and
      the exclusion reasoning;
  (d) the charts, figures and written text of the site.

All of the above are the original work of the rightsholder.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

The underlying United Nations resolutions, decisions and reports are official
United Nations documents. No rights over those texts are claimed here. The
Inter typeface shipped under assets/fonts/ is third-party software under its
own licence; see NOTICE and assets/fonts/Inter-LICENSE.txt.

GRANT

No licence is granted. The work is published for consultation, citation and
scholarly scrutiny. In particular, and without limiting the rightsholder's
rights, the following require prior written authorisation:

  - reproduction, adaptation, translation or redistribution of the code, the
    coding scheme or the coded dataset, in whole or in part;
  - extraction or re-utilisation of a substantial part of the database, whether
    by repeated systematic extraction or otherwise;
  - text and data mining of any part of the work;
  - use of any part of the work for the training, fine-tuning, evaluation or
    grounding of artificial-intelligence models.

Reading the site, quoting it with attribution for research, teaching,
journalism or review, and indexing it in a search service that cites and links
to the source, require no authorisation.

RESERVATION OF TEXT AND DATA MINING RIGHTS

Text and data mining rights are expressly reserved under article 4(3) of
Directive (EU) 2019/790, article L.122-5-3 of the French Intellectual Property
Code and article 67 of the Spanish Consolidated Copyright Act. The same
